According to the Huntik Foundation records, there were once hundreds of Kipperin Titans used by Seekers; however, most of their Amulets became either lost or hidden. {{source|Huntik.com}}

A Kipperin previously belonged to the father of [[Lok Lambert]], [[Eathon Lambert]], who at some point hid Kipperin's Amulet, along with [[Eathon Lambert's journal|his journal]], inside of an old vase. The vase was eventually stored in [[Lok's dormitory]], where Kipperin's Amulet lay dormant until, one day, it was found by Lok, after attempting to stop [[Sophie Casterwill]] from taking the vase down causing it to smash. Kipperin's power instantly syncronized with Lok, and later saved his life by guiding him safely through the air as he ran from the [[Suits]] of the [[the Organization]]. {{source|A Seeker is Born}}

Kipperin first was invoked by Lok in the [[Golem's Attic]] on the [[Road of Alchemists]] when [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] team was nearly defeated by [[DeFoe]]. Lok flew in on Kipperin's wings to take out an Organization operative and help the team to recover [[Metagolem|Metagolem's]] Amulet. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}}

Lok next invoked Kipperin during the battle in the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]], to help dodge the high-powered water blasts from the magical [[Gargoyle]] trap. After getting hit, Kipperin returned to his Amulet. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}} Kipperin later saved Lok's life after he fell into a trap accidentally set of by [[Peter]] while venturing into a hidden chamber. {{source|Crawling the Catacombs}} Kipperin was used in the French catacombs to help Lok escape a group of Suits. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}

Kipperin was used in [[Iceland]] to lift [[Ignatius]] to make a rainbow, forming the [[Rainbow Bridge]] to the [[Temple of Thor]]. {{source|The Legacy of Thor}} Lok later used him to dodge [[Ymir]]'s attacks in the [[Temple of Thor]] while buying Dante and [[Montehue]] time to utilize [[Mjolnir]]. {{source|Two Powers Become One}}

Kipperin was invoked by Lok to save Dante from falling into a blazing fire whilst battling Rassimov at [[the Professor's castle]]. He was however defeated by [[Rassimov]]'s [[Drybite]] power. {{source|The Divine Comedy}} Lok used Kipperin to return to the final battle against [[the Professor]] but was hauled down by the Mastermind power of [[Araknos]]. After Cherit broke Araknos' control, Kipperin lifted Lok to speak to face to face with [[Overlos]], now under the control of [[Dendras|Dendras's]] string, and banish him to the [[Spirit World]] with three other Legendary Titans. {{source|The Mission}}

Following the defeat of [[the Professor]], Kipperin became Powerbonded with Lok during the Huntik team's mission to [[Peru]] to find out Eathon Lambert's fate. Although at first surprised at Kipperin's sudden transformation, Lok was quickly able to tap into their newly strengthened mental link and immediately went about defeating a group of Suits under [[Wilder]]'s command. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

[[File:S2E30 Lok Kipperin Light Burst.jpg|thumb|Lok and Powerbonded Kipperin using his '''Light Burst''' ability]]
When the bond with his Seeker, [[Lok Lambert]], became stronger, Kipperin gained the ability of [[Powerbonding]] with his Seeker. Kipperin gained the '''Winged Fusion''' ability, allowing him to become a protective armor for his Seeker. In this ability, Kipperin's head turns into the helmet while his wings become cape-like when unused, his tendrils wrapping around his Seeker's limbs and fusing to become the armor. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}} Other Powerbonded abilities include:
*'''Light Burst''' - allows Kipperin to emit yellow energy which can add power to an aerial tackle. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}
*'''Wing Slap''' - allows Kipperin to smack his enemies with his wings, as its name suggests. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Lok has also taken to using Kipperin's '''Winged Fusion''' alongside the [[Willblade]], a powerful combination that has proven a match for many opponents ranging from [[Efreet King]] to [[Legion]]. {{source|The Spiral War}} {{source|Rassimov's Secret}}
